/* inside-the-altimeter */
sec('Altimeter Setting Procedures','How the altimeter works',[dzF('Inside the altimeter','<g class="pdg"><rect x="20" y="14" width="284" height="160" rx="12" fill="var(--surface-2)" stroke="var(--ink-2)" stroke-width="1.6"/><text x="32" y="32" class="d1">sealed instrument case, filled with static air</text><path d="M60 174V196" stroke="var(--accent)" stroke-width="6"/><path d="M60.0 196.0L60.0 186.1" stroke="var(--accent)" stroke-width="1.4" fill="none"/><path d="M60.0 178.0L56.4 186.1L63.6 186.1Z" fill="var(--accent)"/><text x="70" y="194" class="d2" style="fill:var(--accent)">from the static vent on the outside of the aircraft</text><path d="M66 108L74 100L82 108L90 100L98 108L106 100L114 108L122 100L130 108L138 100L146 108V116L138 124L130 116L122 124L114 116L106 124L98 116L90 124L82 116L74 124L66 116Z" fill="var(--surface)" stroke="var(--ink)" stroke-width="1.4" stroke-linejoin="round"/><text x="106" y="115" text-anchor="middle" class="d2">near vacuum</text><path d="M106 124V174" stroke="var(--ink-2)" stroke-width="4"/><path d="M152.0 104.0L152.0 97.8" stroke="var(--bad)" stroke-width="1.2" fill="none"/><path d="M152.0 90.0L148.5 97.8L155.5 97.8Z" fill="var(--bad)"/><path d="M152.0 120.0L152.0 126.2" stroke="var(--bad)" stroke-width="1.2" fill="none"/><path d="M152.0 134.0L155.5 126.2L148.5 126.2Z" fill="var(--bad)"/><text x="158" y="96" class="d2" style="fill:var(--bad)">expands as</text><text x="158" y="106" class="d2" style="fill:var(--bad)">you climb</text><text x="32" y="146" class="d2">aneroid capsule: sealed,</text><text x="32" y="156" class="d2">air removed, spring-held</text><path d="M106 100V64H170" stroke="var(--ink)" stroke-width="1.6" fill="none"/><circle cx="178" cy="64" r="9" fill="none" stroke="var(--ink)" stroke-width="2" stroke-dasharray="2.4 1.6"/><circle cx="198" cy="64" r="6" fill="none" stroke="var(--ink)" stroke-width="2" stroke-dasharray="2 1.4"/><text x="188" y="50" text-anchor="middle" class="d2">linkage and gearing</text><path d="M204 64H236" stroke="var(--ink)" stroke-width="1.6"/><circle cx="262" cy="96" r="30" fill="#151a22"/><path d="M262 96L280 76" stroke="#fff" stroke-width="2"/><circle cx="262" cy="96" r="3" fill="#888"/><path d="M236 64Q262 64 262 93" stroke="var(--ink)" stroke-width="1.2" fill="none" stroke-dasharray="3 2"/><text x="262" y="142" text-anchor="middle" class="d2">pointers</text></g>','The capsule is sealed with most of the air removed, and a spring stops it collapsing. Static air fills the case around it. As you climb, static pressure falls, the capsule expands, and the gearing turns the pointers. (The textbook simplifies this as "a fixed amount of air in the capsule".)',320,204)]);
